{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/853602-lawrence-darkling-hunterheart-trying-to-give-him-a-mein","id":853602,"title":"Lawrence, Darkling Hunterheart... trying to give him a mein.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-26T11:52:25-07:00","id":853602,"title":"Lawrence, Darkling Hunterheart... trying to give him a mein.","content":"So the idea is that Lawrence is a Hunter (probably 1st tier) who followed the trail of a monster straight into the hedge and into his keeper's waiting arms. His keeper transformed him (slowly) into a hunter of other Lost, and he's effectively the antagonist in a Slasher flick. we know that his clothes are always blood spattered and his eyes are cold (he can't help but look at people like they're objects) but beyond that we (his player, Megan, and I) are having a hard time visualizing his fae aspect. <br /> <br /> \u200bany ideas?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T13:50:41-07:00","id":853659,"title":"","content":"How about something like this?<br /> <br /> Lawrence's smooth, pale face shows no remorse and little emotion, his solid black eyes seemingly plucked directly from the face of a shark. An assortment of odd, fleshy trophies hang from a belt above his blood-stained hunting gear, and the blood on his clawed hands always seems fresh. He moves almost silently, and he lacks many of the subtle movements and gestures that most mortals and changelings exhibit. Even in the strongest of winds, his hair does not move in the slightest.<br /> <br /> Are these the sort of images you're looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:45:25-07:00","id":853687,"title":"","content":"Pretty much, we were thinking about the mask-like appearance too. Also, that he never seems to run, he just walks with purpose and (should you be running from him) never seems too far behind. Thanks!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:02:16-07:00","id":853831,"title":"","content":"When designing a Darkling Hunterheart, I borrowed influences from Cenobites.<br /> <br /> Perhaps for your character, some Friday the 13th influence, maybe his mien is a blood splattered hockey mask, that never comes off because it is his face. And blood always drips from his fingers, only evaperating when he leaves an area, as the blood is just a part of his mien.<br /> <br /> Also concider that court mantle and his contracts can influence and twist his mien as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:53:57-07:00","id":853893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/853602-lawrence-darkling-hunterheart-trying-to-give-him-a-mein?p=853659#post853659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lawrence's smooth, pale face shows no remorse and little emotion, his solid black eyes seemingly plucked directly from the face of a shark.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI might take the shark aspect even further, depending on his hunting/killing methods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/>